+// The clustered scene shader historically used subgroup reductions to make every
+// lane in a subgroup walk the SAME cluster item range, so the loop branches
+// coherently. That is a divergence optimisation, not a correctness requirement:
+// each lane already holds its own correct item_from/item_to and its own mask.
+//
+// WebGPU exposes subgroups only as an optional feature, and Tint rejects the
+// unguarded calls ("subgroupOr must only be called from subgroup uniform control
+// flow") -- which fails the whole scene shader, leaves the cluster builder
+// uncreated, and makes Forward+ draw nothing. Defining the reductions as identity
+// lets each lane use its own value: the same lights, decals and reflections are
+// gathered, just with less coherent branching. Correct everywhere.
+#define subgroupBroadcastFirst(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupMin(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupMax(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupOr(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupElect() (true)
 
